TITLE:: TunnelPanel
summary:: Tunnel's device panel, with a hand from the display to the knobs
categories:: Libraries>Tunnel
related:: Classes/Tunnel, Classes/TunnelView, Classes/FxDevicePanel, Classes/FxDeviceGUI

DESCRIPTION::
The link::Classes/FxDevicePanel:: every effect of the family has - header, display with the in and out meters, pages of cards, the output card, the hint bar - built from Tunnel's table and code::*devicePages::, plus what ties its display to its knobs: the link::Classes/TunnelView:: is given the panel, so hovering the echoes lights the knobs that place them, the gate and duck knobs show the input against their thresholds, and a drag in the display speaks in the hint bar; the knobs of what the display draws light their part of it while hovered.

It is code::Tunnel.panelClass::, so code::gui:: and code::panel:: both make one; everything else is link::Classes/FxDevicePanel::'s.

code::
t = Tunnel.new;
t.gui;                  // in its own window (FxDeviceGUI)

(
w = Window("tunnel", Rect(100, 100, 960, 560));
p = t.panel(w);         // or in yours
w.layout = VLayout(p.view);
p.running = true;
w.onClose = { p.remove };
w.front;
);
::

CLASSMETHODS::

METHOD:: new
ARGUMENT:: unit
The link::Classes/Tunnel::.
ARGUMENT:: parent
A view to go in.

INSTANCEMETHODS::

METHOD:: hints
The hint bar: setting it also attaches the knobs that light their part of the display.
